{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/519588-mummies-and-the-creation-of-the-sahara","id":519588,"title":"Mummies and the Creation of the Sahara","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-19T08:10:21-07:00","id":519588,"title":"Mummies and the Creation of the Sahara","content":"Well, I seem to have royally messed up the last time I started this thread, so sorry for the double post, and let's try this again...<br /> <br /> Alright, so I've been working on a timeline of both real world history and the history of the World of Darkness, both out of interest, and because it results in some neat plot ideas for when I'm storytelling. I think I've found yet another one.<br /> <br /> Here are some baseless assumptions I've made before I start detailing it:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The Nameless Empire lasted less than a full Sothic Turn and while it was a long lived Empire, due to supernatural aid and being fairly well run, it was still comparable to some real long lasting empires and nations.</li> <li>The Rite of Return began about a century before it was completed, but the final true ritual occurred in 3832 BCE, when Irem vanished, on the Sothic Turn.</li> <li>Azer's murder occurred exactly one Sothic turn before Irem's fall.</li> </ol>Using these, and some of my own creative license, I've come up with this section of Mummy dates which are in gold (it seemed appropriate):<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://orig15.deviantart.net/9dc2/f/2015/139/c/a/nameless_empire_and_5_9_ky_event_by_peace__out-d8tybvq.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Purple are nations/civilizations/culture groups. Blue are historical events and time periods. What's most interesting to me right now, and what I discovered today through some research, is on the bottom in brown, which is code for geological events.<br /> <br /> This all comes out of being introduced to the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sahara_pump_theory\" target=\"_blank\">Sahara Pump Hypothesis</a>, which helps to explain human migration out of Africa based on climate change. Basically, the Sahara hasn't always been desert and it goes through cycles. When it is in its wet phase, its more like a savannah, and humans migrate into it, but when it switches back to a desert, they all hightail it for better places to live (unless you are on the Nile). The last time it switched over was during what is known as the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/5.9_kiloyear_event\" target=\"_blank\">5.9 KY Event</a>. This event created the Sahara as we know it today, a dry desert that is very tough to live in. Since we don't actually know when it was, I've put error bars of about plus/minus one hundred years on my timeline, although I may trim that down.<br /> <br /> Point is, this matches the timeline of Irem's fall pretty closely. A later event, the 4.2 KY Event, also on the graph, is widely believed to have lead to the fall of Old Kingdom Egypt (protip: century long droughts in the desert are not fun). Could it be 5.9 KY changed the lives of our Mummies? Could the Rite of Return been responsible for the event itself? What would Irem have been like if the Sahara were more habitable? I know these questions aren't for everyone and that's okay. Use as much or as little historical accuracy in your games as you like. I'm intrigued by these possibilities though and would love to hear other's thoughts on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T09:13:07-07:00","id":519647,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the metaphysical mojo they were using for the RoR leeched the vitality out of the whole Sahara region or something? Maybe this could have something to do with the reality quake that destroyed Atlantis, I dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T10:26:34-07:00","id":519706,"title":"","content":"See that far left line, at 5500 BCE? That's when Neolithic Mage is set.<br /> <br /> Atlantis was destroyed before it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T10:31:53-07:00","id":519707,"title":"","content":"Given the quantum screwery going on, wouldn't it be more accurate to say Atlantis wasn't built before then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T10:47:04-07:00","id":519759,"title":"","content":"People assume that Atlantis is a strict progression of cause to affect, but actually, from a non-linier, non subjective point of view it is more like a big ball of wibbily wobbly Antlantisy Tantisy...stuff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T10:50:25-07:00","id":519769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/519588-mummies-and-the-creation-of-the-sahara?p=519706#post519706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See that far left line, at 5500 BCE? That's when Neolithic Mage is set.<br /> <br /> Atlantis was destroyed before it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that it never existed in the current iteration of the nWoD universe, I think that's a no-brainer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T10:53:07-07:00","id":519770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/519588-mummies-and-the-creation-of-the-sahara?p=519759#post519759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People assume that Atlantis is a strict progression of cause to affect, but actually, from a non-linier, non subjective point of view it is more like a big ball of wibbily wobbly Antlantisy Tantisy...stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>Just <i>once</i> I would like to have a conversation about time that didn't involve Blink.<br /> <br /> But whatever, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T10:59:40-07:00","id":519774,"title":"","content":"Well I was just taking a jovial tone, and I haven't read much of Mummy yet, something I'm in the process of correcting, but I thought that Mage was generally pretty clear that at some point there was a precursor culture of mages who current mages believe lived in a golden age whose central city they now refer to as Atlantis. However, the word Atlantis is more a word just used as a place holder to convey the idea of a perfected mage society. Also there are some societies and groups within the MtAw setting actually don't believe that Atlantis has even existed yet since the shattering of the ladder was such a powerful and resonant action that it echoes across all of time simultaneously. Hence the ladder is always breaking, has always been broken and is yet to break.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","user":"Gullinbursti","date":". 05-19-2015, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T11:36:05-07:00","id":519811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/519588-mummies-and-the-creation-of-the-sahara?p=519647#post519647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the metaphysical mojo they were using for the RoR leeched the vitality out of the whole Sahara region or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the first thing I jumped to too, but there are other questions as well, like how far did the Nameless Empire stretch? Up until now, my assumption has been that Irem followed the same rule as the all of the Nile Kingdoms since the Old Kingdom... namely that the Kingdom was bound to the Nile. If we are talking an era when the Wadis are actually connected into rivers we could be looking at a kingdom stretching across North Africa to the West, and Arabia to the east, since the Empty Quarter was likely created by the same event. <br /> <br /> Then there is yet more memory trauma for our Mummy &quot;heroes&quot; in the First Sothic Turn. I've been in the Sahara and the dunes are massive, they could easily swallow entire towns. Imagine a Mummy that arose somewhere far from Egypt, like Cyprus, or even in the Indus Valley. The Mummy builds its cult, and at the same time, slowly, carefully, rebuilds its memory. It has just enough to remember where it was born and raised before the Blessed Ones called it to its eternal duty. It wasn't far from the Nile, poised on a small tributary that made lush, green farmland with black soil out of the savannah. The Mummy pieces its location back together and braves the elements, its rivals, and the unliving to catch glimpse of where its journey started so that a new destination can be determined. <br /> <br /> When the Mummy arrives though, there is nothing. Less than that even. Oh, the Nile is still strong, but the tributary is gone. Farmland is there, but it only comes from one river now. The Mummy's birthplace is now well out of the floodzone, and the Savannah is long gone. Now there is only sand. Instead of a town, there a dune many times the size of the town, and far bigger than its tallest building. <br /> <br /> There is no beginning for the Mummy anymore. The world has moved one. It has just awakened, and it is even more a relic than the trinkets it seeks out for its Judge. <br /> <br /> To me, that just adds a whole new level horrible to the Curse that was already one of the worst in the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T12:07:32-07:00","id":519830,"title":"","content":"As I said, I'm not widely read on Mummy yet, but this note of melancholy and loss is one of the things that is attracting me to the setting on the first read through. It seems, even when compared to the Kindred, these are the true eternal supernaturals of the World of Darkness and as such, they are the ones who lose the most as they continue down an endless path of death and rebirth. I really like using musical allusion in my chronicles and I think, even at this point, that my first chronicle's name would be Dust in the Wind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T18:00:55-07:00","id":520253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/519588-mummies-and-the-creation-of-the-sahara?p=519647#post519647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the metaphysical mojo they were using for the RoR leeched the vitality out of the whole Sahara region or something? Maybe this could have something to do with the reality quake that destroyed Atlantis, I dunno.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;My brothers and sisters prepare a Rite of Return. You and your demons stalk invisible places and you, a god, were made with the mysteries of the Judges in your heart. So yes, I come to you in ignorance, for <b>I would know the nature of this spell.</b>\u201d<br /> <i><b>That tendril of the Devourer? </b>I know it. I see her black threads grow stronger as you and your mortal playthings will them into shape, and bind them with your tools and Utterances. I see beyond the horizon of time, when the threads become a hand smothering the world.</i></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T18:11:08-07:00","id":520274,"title":"","content":"See, Bale Hounds are gonna win.<br /> <br /> Is Abdju, the Hill of Relics, related to the Abedju Cipher?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-19-2015, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T20:16:01-07:00","id":520375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/519588-mummies-and-the-creation-of-the-sahara?p=520274#post520274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, Bale Hounds are gonna win.<br /> <br /> Is Abdju, the Hill of Relics, related to the Abedju Cipher?</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea! I'd have have never picked up on it if you hadn't mentioned it, since I'm only just getting into Mage! The only reference I've since is from Sothis Ascends, although now I'm going to have to look it up and dig into the history of Abydos some more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T20:32:50-07:00","id":520385,"title":"","content":"I think it was an ancient Egyptian artifact. I used the SAS for a hunter game, so I don't remember a lot of the mage related details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T23:54:15-07:00","id":520589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/519588-mummies-and-the-creation-of-the-sahara?p=519647#post519647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the metaphysical mojo they were using for the RoR leeched the vitality out of the whole Sahara region or something? Maybe this could have something to do with the reality quake that destroyed Atlantis, I dunno.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fun to consider Ki-En-Gir and the mythology of ancient Sumeria when examining this question.<br /> <br /> Sumerians believed very strongly in water as a fundamental aspect of the universe. They kinda literally believed fish people emerged from the deeps to give them learning and religion. nWoD actually references this in the fish-shifter write up, but that's really a sidebar to my final point here - anyway, the primary Sumerian Ziggurut was connected to this elemental plane of water, essentially, where all the Gods lived with enlightened fish mystics. The guy who was in charge of it was literally in charge of... wait for it... flooding.<br /> <br /> So what would happen to the world if you say, grabbed that guy and ripped his heart out so you could have a chat with Ammut? Hmmmm. The ancient Sumerians believed this guy was who kept the seasons in check, who kept the flooding of the Tigris and Euphrates under control...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T00:11:03-07:00","id":520613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/519588-mummies-and-the-creation-of-the-sahara?p=520589#post520589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's fun to consider Ki-En-Gir and the mythology of ancient Sumeria when examining this question.<br /> <br /> Sumerians believed very strongly in water as a fundamental aspect of the universe. They kinda literally believed fish people emerged from the deeps to give them learning and religion. nWoD actually references this in the fish-shifter write up, but that's really a sidebar to my final point here - anyway, the primary Sumerian Ziggurut was connected to this elemental plane of water, essentially, where all the Gods lived with enlightened fish mystics. The guy who was in charge of it was literally in charge of... wait for it... flooding.<br /> <br /> So what would happen to the world if you say, grabbed that guy and ripped his heart out so you could have a chat with Ammut? Hmmmm. The ancient Sumerians believed this guy was who kept the seasons in check, who kept the flooding of the Tigris and Euphrates under control...</div> </div> </div> </div>That definitely has some cool implications there! From what I've read in the last day and a bit, the 5.9 Kiloyear event did impact the Arabian Peninsula, so its not inconceivable of having reached all the way to Sumeria.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https: